{
  "id": "2026-10-13-plug-in-solar",
  "title": "Solar panels you plug into the wall are catching on",
  "topic": "일상",
  "level": 2,
  "voice": "en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Today's story is about solar panels you can plug straight into a wall.",
    "People often call it balcony solar, and it's taking off fast.",
    "A typical kit is just one to three panels with a small inverter.",
    "You hang it on a balcony or a fence, plug it into an outlet, and it powers things in your home.",
    "It won't run your whole house, but it can cover ten to thirty percent of a household's electricity.",
    "In Germany, more than a million of these have been installed in just a few years.",
    "Now the idea is catching on in the United States.",
    "Utah was the first state to allow it, in 2025, and nine more states, including California, have followed.",
    "The big selling point is the price.",
    "One renter in Colorado paid under three hundred dollars for a single panel.",
    "They think it has already saved them more than that.",
    "That matters for renters, who usually can't put panels on a roof.",
    "Some utilities worried about safety, but a UK government study found no direct electrical hazard.",
    "Would you try one on your balcony? Tell me why or why not."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "벽 콘센트에 바로 꽂는 1~3장짜리 '베란다 태양광'이 빠르게 퍼지고 있다. 가정 전력의 10~30%를 댄다.",
    "독일은 몇 년 새 100만 대 넘게 설치했고, 미국은 2025년 유타를 시작으로 캘리포니아 등 9개 주가 뒤따라 허용했다.",
    "300달러 미만이라 지붕이 없는 세입자도 쓸 수 있다. 안전 우려가 있었지만 영국 정부 조사에선 직접적 전기 위험이 없었다."
  ],
